<DocsLayout title="Aurora Developer Guide" description="Set up, validate and contribute to the Aurora Website repository." heading="Developer guide" eyebrow="DOCUMENTATION / DEVELOPERS">
<p class="docs-kicker">FOR DEVELOPERS</p>
<h2>Start with the repository you are changing.</h2>
<p>Aurora is developed across separate workstreams. This guide covers the public <a href="https://github.com/Pokejoueur/aurora-website">Aurora Website repository</a>; it does not imply access to private repositories or describe unverified OS or browser APIs.</p>
<div class="docs-callout"><strong>Repository scope</strong><p>Website source: public GitHub repository. Aurora OS: private repository. The browser repository and its implementation details have not been verified by this website workstream.</p></div>
<h2>Requirements</h2>
<ul><li>Node.js 22.22.0 or newer (the repository pins its version in <code>.nvmrc</code>).</li><li>npm, included with Node.js.</li><li>Git and access to the public website repository.</li></ul>
<h2>Clone and run locally</h2>
<pre><code>git clone https://github.com/Pokejoueur/aurora-website.git
cd aurora-website
git switch main
npm install
npm run dev</code></pre>
<p>Open the local URL printed by Astro (normally <code>http://localhost:4321</code>). Keep your changes on a feature branch rather than committing directly to <code>main</code>.</p>
<h2>Validate before opening a pull request</h2>
<pre><code>npm run check
npm run build
npm run preview</code></pre>
<p><code>npm run check</code> validates the public status registry and runs Astro checks. <code>npm run build</code> generates the static site in <code>dist/</code>. <code>npm run preview</code> serves that built output locally; it does not deploy the site.</p>
<h2>Where to make changes</h2>
<ul>
  <li><code>src/pages/en/</code> — English routes and page content.</li>
  <li><code>src/layouts/</code> — shared page and documentation layouts.</li>
  <li><code>src/styles/global.css</code> — global design system and responsive styling.</li>
  <li><code>src/data/status.json</code> — public status claims and evidence references.</li>
  <li><code>docs/</code> — architecture decisions, governance and website roadmap.</li>
  <li><code>public/</code> — static assets and hosting headers.</li>
  <li><code>.github/workflows/ci.yml</code> — automated validation and build.</li>
</ul>
<h2>Contribution workflow</h2>
<ol>
  <li>Inspect the current branch, working tree, relevant page and existing conventions.</li>
  <li>Create a focused branch and make one coherent change.</li>
  <li>Keep product claims tied to evidence from the relevant product repository or test report.</li>
  <li>Run the validation commands and inspect the rendered pages at desktop and mobile widths.</li>
  <li>Review the complete diff for broken links, accessibility regressions, unsupported claims and unrelated changes.</li>
  <li>Open a pull request with its purpose, scope, validation results and known limitations.</li>
</ol>
